  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda: LAND-at-scale: Land Conflict Resolution Project (LCRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To improve understanding by key land security stakeholders of the barriers                limiting inclusive, accessible, transparent and predictable access to land justice through the Abunzi                Committees (ACs) in two (2) pilot districts. 2) To enhance the capacity of the Abunzi, National Land                Authority (NLA) and district staff to make just decisions on land-related disputes. 3) To develop an                operational and efficient Information Management System and quality-control system for land dispute                resolution for the NLA. 4) To increase family councils&#x2019; and justice seekers&#x2019; understanding                of land rights and of the role of the different land dispute resolution actors. 5) To have key                Ministries agree on a road map for sustainable institutionalization and further national scaling of                enhanced land justice via the Abunzi. 6) To inform citiziens, including women and vulnerable groups, in                Gasabo District about their land rights and how to solve their disputes through Alternative Dispute                Resolution (ADR). 7) To improve the capacity of Abunzi, NLA, Access to Justice Bureaus (Maisons d&#x2019;Acc&#xe8;s                &#xe0; la Justice - MAJ), district staff and non-professional bailiffs, to use ADR. 8) To improve                awareness of private sector actors and the Private Sector Federation (PSF) arbitrators on the benefits                of ADR.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ministry of Justice, Ministry of Local Government, Ministry                of Environment, National Land Authority, selected Primary Courts and civil society organizations, Abunzi                and Abunzi Committees, Access to Justice Bureaus (Maisons d&#x2019; Acc&#xe8;s &#xe0; la Justice),                one-stop centres, Cell and sector Land Committees (LC), local authorities in the targeted districts                (mayors and vice mayors), and private sector actors &#x2013; including Private Sector Federation                arbitrators. Indirect beneficiaries: LC members operating in the targeted districts; and communities of                the pilot districts, especially rural women and people suffering land insecurity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance land-related conflict management and dispute resolution                mechanisms at the decentralized level, with the ultimate goal of enhancing land security in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
